## Likely research implications
Such a framework would be expected to:
- optimize grounding conductor arrangement and material usage;
- improve diagnosis of grounding defects or unsafe configurations;
- support case-based reuse of historical grounding solutions;
- enhance fault response through similarity-guided reasoning;
- remain scalable in complex substations and active distribution environments.

## Main challenge areas
The main open issues are:
- heterogeneous and incomplete data;
- computational complexity of coupled simulation-optimization pipelines;
- scalability to large networked substations;
- uncertainty in environmental and operating conditions;
- the need for interpretable similarity metrics and engineering validation.

